If switching from running to gym training this winter has left you stiff, sore or favouring one side, you're not alone, and it's worth getting it looked at properly rather than waiting for it to settle on its own.

At MOSIC, assessment doesn't stop at the sore spot. Practitioners look at the whole chain of movement involved, hips, spine, shoulders and how they work together, to understand why the strain happened in the first place. Treatment is hands-on and can include joint mobilisation and soft tissue work, alongside clear guidance on how to ease back into training without the same issue returning a few weeks later.

Both the Bourke Street clinic in the CBD and the Essendon clinic see this pattern often, particularly around long weekends when training routines change quickly. Telehealth appointments are also available for anyone who'd rather start with a conversation before coming in.

Book online at melbourneosteopathycentre.com.au or call 03 9663 6202.

